  "body": "The v0.14.0 cut wrote RELEASE_NOTES.md as its own section only (no `---` separator, history dropped). `scripts/release.ps1` passed it, the tag was pushed, all five platform builds of release.yml went green, and only the publish job then failed:\n\n```\nRELEASE_NOTES.md has no '---' line: cannot tell this version's notes from the history\n```\n\nThe tag cannot be moved, so the v0.14.0 release had to be published by hand from that run's artifacts; the notes were repaired on main by PR #270.\n\nFix: release.ps1's preflight applies the same three checks the publish step does (a `---` line exists, a non-empty section before it, and the first line names the version), so a cut stops before the bump, not after the tag.\n",
